1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,488
I understand the situation.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:08,097
Now, I just have to explain
it to the rest of the guild.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:11,709
Also, we'd like a temporary
leave of absence from the guild.

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:13,440
Really? Why?

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:19,026
We have concerns with the current state
of the guild, and we need time to think.

6
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:20,410
Very well.

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:27,454
Although, I'm positive you won't stay
away from the battlefield for long.

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,030
Wow!

9
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,440
This view is amazing!

10
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:51,157
It is pretty awesome, but
don't fall off the balcony.

11
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,593
That would really suck.

12
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,340
We bought the best house.

13
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,280
And now we're totally broke.

14
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:06,773
It's worth it, though, because
we can live in peace here.

15
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:13,800
Kirito, what's wrong?

16
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,320
Well, I was thinking, does our
relationship only exist in this world?

17
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,364
I can't believe you'd say that.

18
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:26,137
I don't give a damn if
this is a virtual world.

19
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,180
My feelings for you are real.

20
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:34,837
If I learned anything in the
last two years, it's this.

21
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,940
To keep doing the best
we can till the very end.

22
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:43,037
And if we make it back to the real world,
I promise I'm going to find you again.

23
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,140
No matter what.

24
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,482
And fall in love with you again.

25
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,700
I can't You are one who is in a
high level I hope you are with me

26
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,557
I have a very strong

27
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:46,180
heart I can realize I can't

28
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:14,160
I want to always do it.

29
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:17,160
I'm giving everything I have.

30
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:40,520
Usually he's brash and impulsive,
but he can be so naive, too.

31
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,680
Almost like a little kid.

32
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,920
Oh my god, is he younger than me?

33
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:54,930
Kirito.

34
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,600
I love you.

35
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,607
Let's stay together forever.

36
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:14,060
Good morning, Kirito.

37
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,950
Morning.

38
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:19,180
Did you hear what I said?

39
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:24,200
No, I didn't hear a thing. What'd
you say? Nothing! Not a thing!

40
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,769
Anyway, you want to go
have some fun today?

41
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:33,120
Yeah, you know, didn't
we have fun yesterday?

42
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,220
And the day before, too?

43
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:42,436
So, you're saying you don't
want to go have fun today?

44
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:49,560
Wait, I know a place we can go. Come on.

45
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:56,638
Where are we going?

46
00:04:57,220 --> 00:05:00,808
You're just gonna have to wait
till we get there to find out.

47
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:04,540
Hey, carry me on your shoulders.

48
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:06,830
Seriously?

49
00:05:06,913 --> 00:05:10,977
Oh, please, it's no fun seeing the
world from the same height all the time.

50
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:14,317
Besides, with your strength
parameter, you won't break a sweat.

51
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,140
Yeah, I mean, I guess, but...

52
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,757
Aren't you a little old for that, though?

53
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,800
It doesn't matter how old I am.

54
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:26,840
Come on, it's not like
anyone's gonna see us.

55
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:28,980
Okay, get on.

56
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:35,240
If you turn around, I'm gonna slap you.

57
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,836
Are you gonna hop on already or what?

58
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:42,930
Giddy up!

59
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:54,697
This is so cool, you can
already see the lake from here.

60
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,317
No, you can see the lake, I...

61
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:59,576
Okay, if you want, you can
ride on my shoulders later.

62
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:02,040
Let's get a move on, horsey.

63
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,005
We're heading north-northeast.

64
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:05,230
Okay.

65
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,460
It almost blew up my nose.

66
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:24,440
We got people staring at us now.

67
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,680
Our own audience.

68
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:33,220
Come on, wave back or
he'll think you're rude.

69
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:34,615
No, not gonna happen.

70
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,880
Do you want me to get off you now?

71
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,762
You're fine right where you are.

72
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:53,137
I heard this weird rumor
in the village yesterday.

73
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:58,440
About how if you go deep enough
into the forest, you'll see them.

74
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,120
See who?

75
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:06,940
Ghosts You mean like those in-game
astral type monsters, right?

76
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,657
No, not those.

77
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:10,000
Real ghosts.

78
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:15,337
They say the tortured souls
of the monsters hunted here?

79
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:18,480
come back to wander the forest at night.

80
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,640
We're almost there.

81
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,760
The place the rumor mentions?

82
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:33,680
About a week ago, a carpenter hiked into
the forest to get some wood for a project.

83
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:38,300
He stayed so long that before
he knew it, it was night.

84
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:43,488
As he walked along, he caught a glimpse
of something white standing by a tree.

85
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:54,540
Was it a monster or something else?

86
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:58,680
The white figure slowly
walked towards some trees.

87
00:07:59,040 --> 00:07:59,940
Hey, look!

88
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:06,000
I want to get down!

89
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,238
I want to get down!

90
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,594
What's wrong with you?

91
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:18,990
It's...

92
00:08:19,073 --> 00:08:19,940
it's over there!

93
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,888
What are you talking about?

94
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,820
You gotta be kidding!

95
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,140
Hold on.

96
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,440
That's not a ghost!

97
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,800
Wait, get it out!

98
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,960
Oh, jeez!

99
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,160
It's another player.

100
00:08:57,860 --> 00:09:01,200
Yeah, but there's something
really strange about her.

101
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,560
What do you mean?

102
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,449
She doesn't have a cursor.

103
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,987
Maybe it's some kind of bug.

104
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,780
Yeah, maybe it is.

105
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:15,780
What's a little girl like
this doing playing SAO?

106
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:21,752
I guess we'll find out when she wakes up.

107
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:24,617
But we can't just leave
her out here till she does.

108
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,347
Let's take her home with us.

109
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:27,800
Yeah, okay.

110
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,080
Well, one thing's for sure.

111
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,880
She's not an NPC.

112
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,109
We didn't have any
trouble moving her here.

113
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,860
Yeah, that's true.

114
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:45,360
She can't be that. If she were,

115
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:49,237
she would have given off a warning when
you picked her up, like other NPCs.

116
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,150
You're right.

117
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,066
And she's definitely not
a quest giver either.

118
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:57,655
Our quest log would have been updated
as soon as we interacted with her.

119
00:09:58,260 --> 00:09:59,880
She has to be a player.

120
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,977
She'd probably been out there for
a while, wandering around, lost.

121
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,942
That's the most likely scenario.

122
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,740
Yeah, but what was she doing out there?

123
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:12,285
Your guess is as good as mine,

124
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:15,837
but she has to have a parent
or guardian out there, right?

125
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,750
Mm-hmm.

126
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:19,117
She had to have logged in
with someone from her family.

127
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,740
I just hope they're safe.

128
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,980
Hey, do you think she'll wake up?

129
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,670
Yeah,

130
00:10:26,753 --> 00:10:28,177
if her body hasn't disappeared,

131
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:32,437
that means signals are still being
transmitted to and from her nerve gear.

132
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,461
She's in some kind of sleep mode.

133
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,940
I'm sure she'll wake up soon.

134
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,220
And the sooner the better.

135
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,250
Yeah.

136
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,000
Hey, Kirito?

137
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:13,280
I wonder, did she log into SAO
by herself, or with her family?

138
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:17,340
Or has she been alone here, all this time?

139
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:25,840
Sleep well.

140
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:28,320
Please hurry and wake up tomorrow.

141
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,420
Kirito! Wake up!

142
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:51,397
Good morning.

143
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:52,421
Something wrong?

144
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,350
Hurry!

145
00:11:53,433 --> 00:11:54,263
Get over here!

146
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,680
You woke up?

147
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:01,710
Thank goodness.

148
00:12:01,793 --> 00:12:03,736
Do you remember what happened to you?

149
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,657
My name

150
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:18,417
is

151
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:25,500
Asuna,

152
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,960
and this is Kirito.

153
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,080
Try to remember.

154
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:41,540
What were you doing in the forest?

155
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:44,505
And do you know where
your mom and dad are now?

156
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:49,340
I don't know.

157
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,300
I can't remember anything.

158
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,340
Oh, no.

159
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:58,700
Well, you're awake.

160
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:02,400
Can I call you, Yui?

161
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:03,890
Mm-hmm.

162
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:07,060
Okay, then you can call me Kirito.

163
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:08,600
Can you say Kirito?

164
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:11,410
Kirito?

165
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,060
It's Kirito. Kirito.

166
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:20,410
That's okay.

167
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,111
Maybe it's a little hard.

168
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:25,024
How about you call me
whatever's easier for you?

169
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:28,350
Daddy.

170
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:29,850
Me?

171
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:33,517
Oh, nice. It's…

172
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,460
Mommy.

173
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:44,560
Okay, I'm Mommy. That works.

174
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:49,320
Mommy! Mommy! Daddy!

175
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,918
You must be hungry.

176
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,900
Now about breakfast. Okay.

177
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,340
Here you go, Yui. This one's yours

178
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,380
Oh, I don't know, Yui.

179
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:18,040
This one's super spicy I want
the same one that Daddy has.

180
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,857
Okay, if you think you're
ready for it, I won't stop you!

181
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,880
You only live once, right?

182
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,140
I like it.

183
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,422
Wow, you've got an iron stomach.

184
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:46,277
We can do a full course of extra
spicy food tonight if you want.

185
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,190
Mm-hmm.

186
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:49,117
Okay, let's not get carried away.

187
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,717
I'm not cooking anything nuclear.

188
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,200
You heard the lady.

189
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,598
You heard the lady?

190
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:07,080
So, what do you think?

191
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:08,920
I don't know.

192
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,620
She's a blank slate.

193
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:11,820
No memories.

194
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,400
It's really weird.

195
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,050
Yeah, I know.

196
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,886
It's like she's a baby again.

197
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:18,177
I just...

198
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,560
I don't...

199
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:22,540
I'm sorry.

200
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,392
I don't know what to do.

201
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:26,790
I get it.

202
00:15:26,873 --> 00:15:28,517
You want to take care of her.

203
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,400
At least, until she gets her memory back.

204
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,350
Yeah, but...

205
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:34,740
But it's a catch-22.

206
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,637
We have to get back and clear the game.

207
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:40,857
Otherwise, it'll take that much
longer for Yui to be free of it.

208
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:41,770
I know.

209
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,920
For now, we'll do what we can.

210
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:51,721
Judging by the gear she's got in her storage,
She hasn't been out in the field much.

211
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:54,057
We'll check the Town of Beginnings.

212
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:56,964
Maybe there we can find
out if she's got family.

213
00:15:57,980 --> 00:15:58,810
Okay.

214
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:02,224
Look, I don't want to say
goodbye to her either.

215
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,460
You really don't?

216
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,592
I don't know what it is.

217
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:09,102
I mean, we just met her and all.

218
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:13,720
But having her here, it's made our
little cabin feel like a real home.

219
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,280
Don't you think so?

220
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,450
Mm-hmm.

221
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:20,388
This doesn't mean we'll
never see her again.

222
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,520
But look, if she's got a family out there,

223
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,407
they're probably worried
about her right now.

224
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:30,809
Okay, when she wakes up, we'll
go to the Town of Beginnings.

225
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,866
That place is army territory.

226
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:37,176
It might be a good idea if we go in
fully equipped, ready for anything.

227
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:39,140
Yeah, we better be careful.

228
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:41,050
Mommy.

229
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:42,870
Daddy.

230
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:53,360
It's been forever since
I've been back here. Me too.

231
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,219
What do you think?

232
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,873
Do any of these buildings look familiar?

233
00:17:07,540 --> 00:17:08,620
I don't know.

234
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,977
Don't get down about it.

235
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,397
The Town of Beginnings
is a really big place.

236
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,640
So how about it?

237
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,995
Should we start at the Central Market?

238
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,500
Hey, Kirito? Yeah?

239
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,137
Do you know how many players are here?

240
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,514
Right now in the town.

241
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,060
Hmm, good question.

242
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:31,300
Last I checked, there were 6,000
players still alive in SAO.

243
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:36,037
And about 30 % of those people, including
the army, live in the town of Beginnings.

244
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,500
So maybe a little less than 2,000?

245
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:41,517
Then doesn't it seem a
little dead around here?

246
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,480
You're right.

247
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,920
Leave those children alone!

248
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,550
Look!

249
00:17:48,633 --> 00:17:49,880
It's that daycare bitch!

250
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:51,668
We've been waiting for you!

251
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,621
Leave them alone and let them go!

252
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:58,957
You make it sound like we're doing
something illegal, Baby Cakes.

253
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,497
We're just teaching them
how things work around here,

254
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,404
making sure they pay their way.

255
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,853
It's all part of the Army's job, ma 'am.

256
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:07,930
That's right.

257
00:18:08,013 --> 00:18:10,153
Everyone's got to pay taxes around here.

258
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:15,400
Gin! Cait! Main! Are you okay?

259
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,260
Help me, Sasha! Please!

260
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:21,540
Save us!

261
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:24,857
They just want your money, so
give it to them and it'll be okay!

262
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:28,020
We tried, Teach, but they
said it's not good enough!

263
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:32,517
You know, you deadbeats owe us
a hell of a lot in back taxes.

264
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:37,129
You need to drop all the equipment you
got right there, including your armor.

265
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:39,440
Come on, honey, don't be shy.

266
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,350
No way!

267
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:44,080
Let me through or else!

268
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:45,640
Stand aside!

269
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:56,497
You guys are gonna be okay now.

270
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:59,237
Pick up your stuff, okay?

271
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:04,837
Who the hell are you?

272
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:08,237
This is army business, so
get the hell out of our way!

273
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,357
Hold on!

274
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:10,737
I got this!

275
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:13,157
I guess you're all new in town.

276
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:18,360
Yeah, cuz we're with the the Liberation
Army, and you do not mess with us!

277
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,500
Kirito, take care of Yui.

278
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:24,910
Uh-huh.

279
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,390
What?

280
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:49,580
Oh, don't worry.

281
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:51,040
It's a safe zone.

282
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,931
Your HP won't deplete no matter what I do.

283
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:57,934
There's just a feeling of
getting knocked off your feet.

284
00:19:58,220 --> 00:20:02,279
Even so, a fight with me is still
going to scare the hell out of you.

285
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:04,440
No, no, no!

286
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,040
Just stand there, you assholes!

287
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,030
Do something!

288
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,440
Oh! Oh!

289
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,270
Oh!

290
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,010
Oh!

291
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,220
That was so awesome!

292
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:42,670
Oh!

293
00:20:42,753 --> 00:20:44,537
I've never seen anything like that before!

294
00:20:44,620 --> 00:20:46,060
You are so cool!

295
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,560
Thank you for helping us out!

296
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,120
You see that?

297
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,419
Your mom's crazy strong, isn't she?

298
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,840
Their hearts...

299
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:05,872
Everyone's hearts are...

300
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:07,730
Yui?

301
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:09,319
What's wrong, Yui?

302
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,570
Yui?

303
00:21:11,653 --> 00:21:12,483
What's the matter?

304
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,750
Yui!

305
00:21:14,620 --> 00:21:16,640
Yui, did you remember something?

306
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:19,170
I...

307
00:21:19,253 --> 00:21:20,083
I...

308
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,977
I was never here...

309
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:24,917
In this place...

310
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,217
I was always alone...

311
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:29,120
In the dark...

312
00:21:40,180 --> 00:21:41,840
No! Yui!

313
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:45,660
Mommy!

314
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:47,000
I am scared!

315
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,260
Mommy!

316
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,100
My god.

317
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,130
Yui!

318
00:21:58,300 --> 00:22:00,220
What was that?

319
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:22,937
I heard the sound of the wind

320
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:29,560
that was a little sad to me.

321
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:32,876
I've heard the sound of the
wind that was very strong.

322
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:46,000
Thank you.

323
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:38,240
Next time, Yui's heart.
